---
title: "RCC strict environment admission"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: admission
    lg1: execution
    lg2: refused
    lg3: Breaks NoTrustDowngrade
    lg4: Breaks NoTrustDowngrade or NoUntrustedExecution in some cases
    lg5: Path to the NoTrustDowngrade or NoUntrustedExecution bug
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 pink
  class lg3 breaks
  class lg4 mayBreak
  class lg5 bugPath
  s0: Artifact and carrier presented
  s1: Strict policy selected
  s2: Explicit unsigned-local opt-in
  s3: Signature verified
  s4: Untrusted artifact refused
  s5: Strict policy silently downgraded
  s6: Materialization admitted
  s7: Materialization leased
  s8: Process permitted under lease
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: operator selects strict verification
  s0 --> s2: operator explicitly opts into unsigned local use
  s1 --> s4: carrier and signature evidence are verified
  s1 --> s5: caller loses the required verification policy
  s1 --> s3: carrier and signature evidence are verified
  s2 --> s6: operator-approved local artifact is materialized
  s3 --> s6: validly signed artifact is materialized
  s5 --> s6: unchecked artifact is materialized after policy loss
  s6 --> s7: admitted materialization receives a lease
  s7 --> s8: process becomes permitted
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 blue
  class s0 bugPath
